s390: Move CIF flags to struct pcpu

jira KERNEL-1869
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9
commit-author Sven Schnelle <svens@linux.ibm.com>
commit d3604ffba1521f59f312be3f19999084dddef446
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-5.14.0-741.7.1.el9_9/d3604ffb.failed

To allow testing flags for offline CPUs, move the CIF flags
to struct pcpu. To avoid having to calculate the array index
for each access, add a pointer to the pcpu member for the current
cpu to lowcore.

	Reviewed-by: Heiko Carstens <hca@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Sven Schnelle <svens@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Vasily Gorbik <gor@linux.ibm.com>
(cherry picked from commit d3604ffba1521f59f312be3f19999084dddef446)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	arch/s390/kernel/smp.c
